  "note": "Posts 1-6 (brand intro) were posted by hand on 15-17 Oct 2026; their colours were cobalt, paper, sun, coral, ink, cobalt. Rebranded to Atelier on 17 Oct 2026: all scheduled posts and reels were re-rendered as *-v2 files and swapped in Metricool; posts 1-6 and 28 stay in the old style. Same evening the headline serif changed from Instrument Serif to Fraunces: scheduled items re-rendered as *-v3. 17 Oct evening: posts 1-6 and 28 recreated in the new style and republished via Metricool; Geoffry archives the old versions by hand. To keep October at 20 published items, posts 08, 12, 17 and 18 became Metricool drafts (reuse later). 17 Oct 22:40: pivot to three stock pieces (planter, bud vase, coasters), no customisation, slogan 'Made in layers. Made in Lebanon.'. All 20 scheduled items (19 Oct-9 Nov) replaced with product-free posts and Reels (brand_posts_launch.py, reels_brand.py); media pinned to commit d14beac. Drafts 08, 12, 17, 18 are retired (they promise custom work): do not reuse. 18 Oct weekly plan: October is at 20/20 Metricool items (8 published 17 Oct + 12 scheduled 19-29 Oct), so October Stories go to the hand-posted story kit (ply-story-01..04). November: 8 feed items scheduled 2-9 Nov (post 52 moved to draft on 18 Oct: delivery promise) + 2 Stories (1 Nov, 5 Nov) = 10/20 if 52 is approved, leaving 10 for launch content with real photos after ~10 Nov. The 7 relaunch posts published 17 Oct 18:45-18:57 went out with the OLD captions (names, spare parts, 'Ply makes it yours'): Geoffry should archive them (or edit the captions) by hand. 19 Oct 2026 (Geoffry): renders allowed on Instagram (labelled 3D render), Metricool upgraded to Starter (no monthly cap), rhythm raised to a daily feed post, 2-3 Reels a week and 1-2 Stories a day; old-line-up posts replaced (see status fields); launch tentatively 1 Dec with countdown drafts. Entries with batch rework-2026-10-19 were scheduled that evening.",
